1
00:00:00,066 --> 00:00:00,795
A coffee shop

2
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:02,355
sold 500 cups last month.

3
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:04,275
This month, it sold 1,000!

4
00:00:04,290 --> 00:00:05,320
Sales volume doubled.

5
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:06,555
But the owner discovered

6
00:00:06,570 --> 00:00:08,055
the shop was making less.

7
00:00:08,070 --> 00:00:09,160
Why?

8
00:00:09,270 --> 00:00:11,055
Here is a business concept.

9
00:00:11,070 --> 00:00:12,795
Contribution Margin

10
00:00:12,810 --> 00:00:13,780
Contribution Margin

11
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:14,835
Simply put

12
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:17,500
it is revenue minus variable costs.

13
00:00:17,730 --> 00:00:20,200
More sales do not always leave more money.

14
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:23,500
Let us use hypothetical figures.

15
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:26,260
Last month, a coffee sold for $8.

16
00:00:26,370 --> 00:00:28,575
Ingredients and packaging cost $3.

17
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:30,220
Each cup contributed $5.

18
00:00:30,270 --> 00:00:30,975
At 500 cups

19
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:33,340
total contribution was $2,500.

20
00:00:33,570 --> 00:00:36,100
This month, the owner ran a promotion.

21
00:00:36,210 --> 00:00:37,900
Each cup sold for just $3.

22
00:00:38,010 --> 00:00:39,700
Variable cost was $2.

23
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:41,440
The shop sold 1,000 cups!

24
00:00:41,550 --> 00:00:43,455
But each cup contributed only $1.

25
00:00:43,470 --> 00:00:45,280
Total contribution was just $1,000.

26
00:00:45,330 --> 00:00:46,455
See what happened?

27
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:48,315
Sales volume rose by 100%.

28
00:00:48,330 --> 00:00:51,100
But total contribution fell by 60%.

29
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:53,320
Too many customers were not the cause.

30
00:00:53,550 --> 00:00:54,615
After the price cut

31
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:56,440
each cup left too little behind.

32
00:00:56,910 --> 00:00:59,380
So when judging how a shop is doing

33
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:00,940
do not look only at sales volume

34
00:01:01,050 --> 00:01:02,980
or the length of its queue.

35
00:01:03,330 --> 00:01:04,960
The key is how much each cup

36
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:06,940
actually contributes.

37
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:09,100
This is Business Through Data.
